cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its derived data, please cite it using the metadata in this file."
type: software
title: "Post-service claim denial and orthopaedic network density in Marketplace plans: analysis code, frozen analysis plan and derived data"
version: "1.0.0"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/samersalman/post-service-denial"
authors:
  - family-names: Salman
    given-names: Samer G.
    affiliation: Baylor College of Medicine
abstract: >-
  Analysis code, the frozen statistical analysis plan, derived plan-level data,
  results and figures for an ecological, plan-level cross-sectional study of 2024
  in-network post-service claim denial in Individual-market qualified health plans
  (CMS plan year 2026 Transparency in Coverage public use file) in relation to
  orthopaedic surgeon density in issuers' published provider directories. The
  repository contains no patient data and no clinician names or addresses.
keywords:
  - health insurance claims
  - claim denial
  - ACA Marketplace
  - provider directories
  - network adequacy
  - orthopaedic surgery
  - ecological study
